  "created": "2026-08-19T11:42:53.48Z",
  "description": "Roslyn analyzers that catch dangerous misuse of the PostQuantum.FileEncryption family at compile time, before it ships: hard-coded passphrases (PQFE101), raw private-key bytes written to disk instead of a passphrase-protected key file (PQFE102), discarded encrypt/decrypt/sign/verify tasks whose authentication never completes or fails unobserved (PQFE103), and silently swallowed fail-closed exceptions (PQFE104). Real-world encryption failures come from misuse, not broken primitives — these rules put the library's fail-closed discipline into the IDE. Development-only dependency; adds nothing to your runtime output.",
